{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OnboardingKit has types and views that can be used to tell users about new features and updates in an app. It keeps track of what the user has already seen, so that items are only presented once, with an opt-in to show all items on the first app launch."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Defining-Whats-New","text":"Defining What’s New"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingWhatsNew","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" item describes a feature or change in a certain app version. It has a version, an optional title, a text, and an icon, which basically means that it’s a versioned "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingUsp","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and can be rendered as such:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let items: [OnboardingWhatsNew<Image>] = [","    .init(","        version: \"1.1\",","        title: \"Sync\",","        text: \"Your data now syncs between your devices.\",","        image: Image(systemName: \"icloud\")","    ),","    .init(","        version: \"1.2\",","        title: \"Widgets\",","        text: \"Add widgets to your **Home Screen**.\",","        image: Image(systemName: \"square.grid.2x2\")","    )","]"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Versions are compared numerically, which means that "},{"code":"1.10","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is considered to be after "},{"code":"1.9","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingWhatsNewInfo","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" gathers items and keeps track of the last version that the user has viewed. The version is persisted with the info’s unique "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which means that you can have separate presentations for different features or parts of the app:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let info = OnboardingWhatsNewInfo(id: \"whats-new\", items: items)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The what’s new info value has properties and functions that keeps track of its presentation state and which items should be presented."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Onboarding","text":"Onboarding"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can use a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/Onboarding\/whatsNew(info:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" onboarding to present this information. The onboarding will present its  "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingWhatsNewInfo\/unviewedItems","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", only if  "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingWhatsNewInfo\/shouldBePresented","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and only on first launch if "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingWhatsNewInfo\/showOnFirstLaunch","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It will also call "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingWhatsNewInfo\/markAllItemsAsViewed()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["Onboarding.whatsNew(info: info).tryPresent { items in ... }"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Since items are marked as viewed before the presentation action is called, the onboarding has a separate use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/Onboarding\/WhatsNew\/tryPresent(after:itemsAction:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that returns which items that will be presented."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Views","text":"Views"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingWhatsNewScreen","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" can be used to present a What’s New screen as a stand-alone screen, or as a page in a flow like "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingPageView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"row","columns":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"OnboardingWhatsNewScreen","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"size":1},{"content":[{"syntax":"swift","code":["OnboardingWhatsNewScreen(","    info: info,","    header: {","        Text(\"What's New\")","            .font(.largeTitle)","    },","    footer: {","        Text(\"Thank you for using My App!\")","    },","    item: { item in","        OnboardingUspListItem(usp: item.usp)","    }",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["OnboardingWhatsNewScreen(info: info)","","OnboardingWhatsNewScreen(info: info) { item in","    Label {","        Text(item.text)","    } icon: {","        item.icon","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"}],"size":3}],"numberOfColumns":4},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The screen wraps an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingWhatsNewView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" in a scroll view and an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingPageContent","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Use the view instead when you want to embed the content in a custom layout."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both views implement "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingWhatsNewComponent","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which means that they have the same initializers. Both support providing custom header, footer, and item view builders."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Styling","text":"Styling"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The views can be styled with an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingWhatsNewStyle","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which is applied with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/onboardingWhatsNewStyle(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". It can define the spacing between the header, items, and footer."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default item list can be styled with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/onboardingUspListStyle(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/onboardingUspListItemStyle(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingWhatsNewScreen","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" can also be styled with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/onboardingPageContentStyle(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"t